WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:45.400 --> 01:47.600
Toru has it, too.

01:49.440 --> 01:53.130
Toru. Do you want to rule the world?

01:56.810 --> 01:58.340
The world?

01:58.410 --> 02:02.910
You saw my powers. Use me and
there'll be nothing beyond your grasp.

02:03.280 --> 02:06.910
If you want, I can give the whole world to you.

02:09.520 --> 02:10.620
No, thanks.

02:10.960 --> 02:12.890
I knew you'd say that.

02:13.360 --> 02:16.660
I know of one other human who told me the same.

02:17.070 --> 02:17.860
Who?

02:22.500 --> 02:23.770
Miyako.

02:24.940 --> 02:27.100
Do you want to see her?

02:28.640 --> 02:30.510
Not really.

02:34.320 --> 02:39.280
Our Fox Deity, Breaks a Taboo

02:42.190 --> 02:44.590
I guess I'll make fried rice using some leftovers.

02:44.890 --> 02:47.530
Hey, can you make inarizushi?

02:47.530 --> 02:48.190
What?

02:48.430 --> 02:49.330
Can you make it or not?

02:49.760 --> 02:53.220
Well, yeah. I've basically been
the housewife here for 12 years.

02:53.400 --> 02:56.070
Good. Make some for dinner tonight.

02:56.070 --> 02:59.310
What? Why do you want inarizushi all of a sudden?

02:59.310 --> 03:01.470
Because I'm a fox. That's why.

03:01.880 --> 03:03.680
Oh yeah...

03:03.680 --> 03:07.220
But do you realize how much
of a hassle they are to make?

03:07.220 --> 03:08.710
Let me help.

03:09.950 --> 03:12.690
C-Can you go to the store for me, then?

03:12.690 --> 03:13.860
I swear to fulfill...

03:13.860 --> 03:16.520
I don't need to hear the rest. Just go.

03:22.560 --> 03:27.730
Why are their sizes, shapes, and prices
different when they have the same name?

03:36.210 --> 03:38.010
Hey, Mamorime.

03:38.580 --> 03:39.740
Tenko-sama.

03:39.880 --> 03:43.220
Noboru gave you extra money, right?

03:43.220 --> 03:45.690
There's something I want to buy.

03:45.690 --> 03:46.750
Is it candy?

03:46.960 --> 03:50.290
No, sake. I want you to buy me sake.

03:51.390 --> 03:53.290
Sake?

03:53.960 --> 03:57.570
If possible, I want pure rice sake.
But, I won't be picky.

03:57.570 --> 03:59.190
Just get me the cheapest one here.

03:59.430 --> 04:01.990
Why do you want to drink sake?

04:02.100 --> 04:05.230
Because! Please, Mamorime!

04:06.770 --> 04:08.540
I don't have that much extra...

04:08.680 --> 04:09.840
Thanks!

04:14.020 --> 04:18.750
Tenko-sama almost never asks anyone for favors.

04:24.130 --> 04:25.830
Why hello there, Toru-kun.

04:25.830 --> 04:26.920
How are you?

04:27.100 --> 04:28.060
Hello.

04:28.200 --> 04:33.730
Oh yeah. Can you give a
message to that fox of yours?

04:34.340 --> 04:35.890
What message?

04:42.580 --> 04:44.010
That's the end of it.

04:45.010 --> 04:47.500
What a beautiful fox deity we have here.

04:50.390 --> 04:55.410
There you are. I was worried it wouldn't
work because there wasn't much sake.

04:56.760 --> 04:58.920
Are you the hashihime here?

04:59.430 --> 05:01.260
Yes, that's right.

05:01.860 --> 05:05.560
Boundaries between the living and
dead easily appear near bridges.

05:05.830 --> 05:10.100
And it is my duty to protect that boundary.

05:10.410 --> 05:12.700
Is this place the boundary for this land?

05:13.110 --> 05:14.730
That would be correct.

05:15.240 --> 05:19.300
Have you ever seen the ghost of a
human woman come by around here?

05:20.650 --> 05:24.950
The soul of Takagami Miyako
still wanders these lands.

05:25.890 --> 05:27.220
No.

05:27.220 --> 05:29.850
Have you ever seen the spell of Spirit Passing?

05:30.220 --> 05:36.860
No. I have lived for quite some time,
but that is one I have not seen.

05:37.570 --> 05:41.470
But that cannot be helped, as it is a
taboo spell that manipulates boundaries.

05:42.070 --> 05:43.500
Want me to show it to you?

05:44.170 --> 05:48.680
I have heard that all humans who attempted
the spell of Spirit Passing in these lands...

05:48.680 --> 05:54.910
...had their left arm torn off by
the god Ebisu in punishment.

05:55.320 --> 05:58.620
Unless you also want a body part taken away...

05:58.990 --> 06:00.320
I don't care.

06:01.960 --> 06:04.150
Oh, you still wish to attempt it?

06:05.160 --> 06:07.090
Oh, I sure do.

06:07.160 --> 06:12.030
Is this person worth all the
risk of the Spirit Passing?

06:12.700 --> 06:16.190
No. She's just a friend.

06:16.740 --> 06:19.300
A friend?

06:19.510 --> 06:22.810
Yes. A hopelessly foolish one at that.

06:28.320 --> 06:31.690
Tenko-sama, it has been a while.

06:31.690 --> 06:33.680
Did another priestess die?

06:33.760 --> 06:38.330
Yes. I have brought a new priestess with me today.

06:38.330 --> 06:39.880
Miyako.

06:46.830 --> 06:48.890
It's so cute!

06:50.810 --> 06:53.980
M-M-M-Miyako! What are you doing to the tenko?!

06:53.980 --> 06:57.910
That's the Kugen Fox!
Guardian deity of the Mizuchi! Get off of it!

07:00.350 --> 07:02.370
So this is that fox.

07:02.820 --> 07:05.720
I'm Miyako. Nice to meet you.

07:05.720 --> 07:07.310
Let's be friends, Kugen-chan!

07:09.290 --> 07:12.590
But Kugen-chan sounds like a mouthful.

07:12.590 --> 07:16.430
Kugen... Kugen... I know!

07:16.760 --> 07:18.860
Starting today, you're Ku-chan!

07:22.240 --> 07:28.800
She was the first priestess to call
me anything besides "Tenko-sama."

07:33.080 --> 07:34.010
School?

07:34.250 --> 07:37.050
I'm leaving home to go to college.

07:37.050 --> 07:39.450
That's why I won't be able to see you for a while.

07:41.590 --> 07:44.110
Bye-bye, Ku-chan. Take care, okay?

07:48.630 --> 07:53.030
She was also the first human I spoke to as an equal.

07:53.300 --> 07:57.940
I understand how much you cared for her.

07:57.940 --> 08:02.710
However, it is still not a sufficient
reason to use the spell of Spirit Passing.

08:07.110 --> 08:08.950
Ku-chan's request?

08:08.950 --> 08:11.250
Yup, my request.

08:11.990 --> 08:15.160
So it's true. Foxes really do like fried tofu.

08:15.160 --> 08:18.790
Yup. But why are there so many different shapes?

08:19.590 --> 08:21.030
I'm sorry...

08:21.300 --> 08:26.430
Oh, yeah. I have a message from
the owner of the convenience store.

08:27.030 --> 08:31.200
The moon is going to be full tonight,
but don't try anything funny.

08:32.270 --> 08:34.570
That's what he said. Do you know what he meant?

08:35.280 --> 08:36.710
It's too late for that.

08:37.350 --> 08:38.680
It's nothing.

08:39.450 --> 08:42.540
Anyways, wouldn't it be nice to
eat outdoors once in a while?

08:42.680 --> 08:44.650
That's sudden.

08:46.050 --> 08:47.880
Is it a blackout?

08:56.960 --> 08:59.570
Is this the bank of the Yayoi River?

08:59.570 --> 09:00.560
Isn't it a nice place?

09:00.740 --> 09:03.400
Ku, when did you change into that?

09:03.400 --> 09:06.130
Wow, there's even a mat here.

09:06.340 --> 09:09.310
Look. The moon tonight is beautiful.

09:12.710 --> 09:15.010
You're right. It's a full moon.

09:19.050 --> 09:20.520
Hey, Ku-chan. No fair.

09:20.520 --> 09:22.120
Don't eat before us!

09:22.120 --> 09:25.020
I'm going to dance. I can't do
that on an empty stomach.

09:25.230 --> 09:26.160
Dance?

09:26.230 --> 09:30.330
It'll be a little show. Just sit there and keep eating.

09:30.330 --> 09:34.790
But no matter what happens,
do not get off the mat. Understand?

09:36.140 --> 09:37.900
No matter what happens?

09:38.210 --> 09:39.470
Ku-chan...

09:42.610 --> 09:44.040
A barrier...

10:15.280 --> 10:17.140
It's beautiful.

10:17.140 --> 10:18.130
Yeah.

10:21.420 --> 10:23.510
The air is being purified.

10:27.120 --> 10:29.120
Hi there, my little Mamorime.

10:29.120 --> 10:32.680
Don't look at me like that. You'll hurt my feelings.

10:33.430 --> 10:34.190
Ebisu!

10:34.460 --> 10:36.450
Come on. Say it with a little respect.

10:37.030 --> 10:39.260
But this is something else.

10:39.770 --> 10:41.800
It's almost like a dance from the heavens.

10:41.800 --> 10:46.570
A Spirit Passing from a fox is really rare.
You don't get to see this every day.

10:49.180 --> 10:49.900
That's...

10:51.910 --> 10:53.680
What's a Spirit Passing?

10:54.120 --> 11:00.150
It's the only spell able to pry open boundaries
and it's reserved only for powerful beings.

11:00.150 --> 11:03.990
But the Spirit Passing is a forbidden spell...

11:03.990 --> 11:07.790
What? Is Ku doing something
she's not supposed to?

11:09.200 --> 11:11.960
Yep. It will definitely have to suffer a penalty for it.

11:12.430 --> 11:13.730
A penalty?

11:15.440 --> 11:16.960
What are you going to do, Ebisu?

11:20.880 --> 11:23.440
Tenko-sama is in the middle of the Spirit Passing.

11:23.440 --> 11:26.210
I won't let you go near her right now!

11:30.180 --> 11:31.280
What was that?

11:32.890 --> 11:35.890
Ninja spell, One Minute Paralysis.

11:35.890 --> 11:38.950
Think of it as an extension of the
Shadow Bind from the other day.

11:41.000 --> 11:45.970
You may have a dragon inside you,
but don't forget you're still human.

11:45.970 --> 11:48.040
And that mat is your barrier.

11:48.040 --> 11:50.060
It's dangerous to go outside of it.

11:50.240 --> 11:51.940
Just shut up and stay in there.

11:51.940 --> 11:52.670
Wait!

12:17.800 --> 12:19.230
The winds stopped...

12:25.470 --> 12:27.240
Even the river stopped flowing.

12:27.980 --> 12:30.410
Now you've done it, you damn fox.

12:34.880 --> 12:36.350
Ku-chan's face!

12:36.350 --> 12:38.720
Is she all right?!

12:38.720 --> 12:41.780
She may have drained herself of her powers...

12:42.060 --> 12:44.090
Well done, fox.

12:44.090 --> 12:49.230
Spirit Passing is a difficult spell,
so I thought you wouldn't succeed.

12:49.230 --> 12:51.000
But you proved me wrong.

12:51.000 --> 12:52.730
Now the lock of the boundary has been released.

12:53.930 --> 12:57.000
But the gate is still closed.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.340
Is it any surprise?

12:58.340 --> 13:03.300
As the local god here, I don't want the boundary
opened up when it's not even the Equinox.

13:03.780 --> 13:09.680
I adjusted the flow of the spirits, magnetic
fields, and underground veins the way I like 'em.

13:09.950 --> 13:14.410
As long as I'm here, I won't let you open it.

13:14.490 --> 13:16.460
Then I'll do it over your dead body.

13:21.300 --> 13:22.000
Ku!

13:22.000 --> 13:22.800
Ku-chan!

13:22.800 --> 13:25.630
Stay in there! Mamorime! Don't let them out!

13:25.900 --> 13:26.830
I can't!

13:27.100 --> 13:28.570
It's dispelled?

13:28.840 --> 13:30.400
Noboru-sama! Toru-sama!

13:30.400 --> 13:31.500
Please wait!

13:32.240 --> 13:37.700
You're nothing but a makeshift guardian deity.
Do you think a fake can defeat a real god?

13:38.050 --> 13:41.010
Fakes have their pride.

13:43.880 --> 13:47.840
The black mist emitted by a
fox is of the metal affinity...

13:48.260 --> 13:51.090
Uh, what was the rest? I completely forgot.

13:52.330 --> 13:54.920
What's this? You make this so easy.

13:58.070 --> 13:59.100
No!

13:59.100 --> 14:01.840
We have to go help Ku-chan!

14:01.840 --> 14:03.600
You shouldn't cross the barrier!

14:03.600 --> 14:05.160
What happens if we go outside of it?

14:05.410 --> 14:07.810
The boundary is partially open, so um...

14:07.810 --> 14:13.910
Living people will go scrunch
and then swirl, and finally fly off.

14:14.110 --> 14:15.170
To where?

14:15.420 --> 14:18.280
That freak of a fox...

14:20.650 --> 14:23.350
The first one was just a dummy.

14:25.390 --> 14:27.620
I got a question for you, fox.

14:27.900 --> 14:32.300
You know who is the one able to manipulate
spiritual powers best in this land?

14:34.130 --> 14:36.860
The answer is me.

14:37.170 --> 14:38.260
Me.

14:38.610 --> 14:41.840
Tenko Kugen. Come here!

14:44.580 --> 14:46.310
He used the kotodama!

14:46.810 --> 14:49.880
Kugen, lift this fog!

14:49.880 --> 14:51.040
Never!

14:52.790 --> 14:54.810
Dammit!

14:57.860 --> 14:59.260
Ku-chan!

14:59.260 --> 15:00.590
She's okay!

15:00.590 --> 15:02.490
Or maybe not.

15:02.930 --> 15:07.170
You already know your powers have been depleted.

15:07.170 --> 15:11.830
You're in a losing battle. So, why?

15:12.640 --> 15:13.630
Because...

15:13.870 --> 15:17.980
Then you're going to have to pay
a fine as heavy as your crime.

15:17.980 --> 15:20.640
You're not taking a body part.
I'll kill myself before I let you do that.

15:21.850 --> 15:22.840
I'll settle for your hair.

15:23.150 --> 15:24.050
My hair?

15:24.390 --> 15:28.990
You went off to perform Spirit Passing
mostly because of what I said.

15:28.990 --> 15:31.220
I'm just taking that into account.

15:31.590 --> 15:34.700
What are you thinking, you worthless god?!

15:34.700 --> 15:36.790
You're horrible! I hope your
store gets run into the ground!

15:37.100 --> 15:40.160
Oh, come on. Your hair grows back, doesn't it?

15:40.730 --> 15:42.730
And it doesn't hurt when it gets cut off.

15:43.040 --> 15:43.700
No.

15:44.070 --> 15:44.970
Gimme.

15:45.210 --> 15:46.070
Never!

15:46.470 --> 15:47.770
I said, give it to me.

15:48.010 --> 15:51.440
The thought of giving
anything to you pisses me off!

15:51.810 --> 15:54.780
Primordial Earth-3, Primordial Heaven-6.
Primordial Earth-1, Manifested Earth-3.

15:58.420 --> 16:00.820
You still have enough power left to cast a spell?!

16:02.220 --> 16:04.750
Manifested Earth-2, Primordial Earth-5,
Manifested Earth-5, Primordial Earth-8!

16:11.570 --> 16:14.360
Seems you can't even maintain
a human face any longer.

16:15.170 --> 16:17.810
I was just trying to talk up a deal with you.

16:17.810 --> 16:19.430
You leave me no choice.

16:24.910 --> 16:26.680
The komainu from Hashiba Shrine!

16:26.680 --> 16:28.710
They were okay.

16:29.150 --> 16:33.450
If you won't give me your hair, I'll take the
lives of those two brothers as a substitute.

16:34.490 --> 16:39.450
The souls of the Mizuchi's descendants
should be a worthy substitute for your hair.

16:39.660 --> 16:40.960
You coward!

16:41.100 --> 16:41.960
Kill them!

16:44.370 --> 16:46.330
We should talk it over, too.

16:46.530 --> 16:49.230
Is this from the Meringue
Shoppe? Or from Hagizushi?

16:49.440 --> 16:50.870
My brother made it by hand.

16:50.970 --> 16:54.140
This looks very good.
It's like something you'd buy at a store.

16:54.140 --> 16:55.110
Thanks.

16:55.310 --> 16:57.000
Time to eat!

16:57.880 --> 16:58.500
Delicious!

16:59.010 --> 17:01.210
Hey, get to work!

17:01.780 --> 17:02.650
Yes, sir!

17:07.820 --> 17:09.480
Please don't take this personally.

17:10.160 --> 17:12.660
After eating everything, you're still...

17:12.660 --> 17:14.820
I won't let you hurt them!

17:20.170 --> 17:20.470
- Do it!

17:20.470 --> 17:21.090
- Wait!
- Do it!

17:24.810 --> 17:25.830
I'll give it to you!

17:26.310 --> 17:27.600
You just want my hair, right?!

17:27.880 --> 17:29.640
That's perfectly fine with me!

17:29.640 --> 17:35.380
Now if only you agreed earlier, we wouldn't
have gotten so nasty with each other.

17:43.920 --> 17:45.130
What a waste.

17:45.130 --> 17:47.860
You didn't have to cut your hair for Ebisu.

17:50.300 --> 17:52.160
Wow, thanks!

17:52.370 --> 17:53.970
What are you plotting?

17:53.970 --> 17:59.670
How rude! The only thing I care about is the
peace and health of the people in my land.

17:59.970 --> 18:00.940
Liar!

18:01.110 --> 18:02.440
I'm not lying...

18:02.440 --> 18:03.880
Well, see you later!

18:04.080 --> 18:04.980
Let's go!

18:04.980 --> 18:05.450
- Yes, sir!

18:05.450 --> 18:06.310
- Right away!
- Yes, sir!

18:10.080 --> 18:11.050
- Ko-chan!
- Ko!

18:14.520 --> 18:16.660
Is Ko-chan going to be okay?

18:16.660 --> 18:19.520
She was protecting the barrier.
Of course she'll be tired.

18:19.930 --> 18:23.450
You should be tired, too. Are you okay, Ku?

18:24.300 --> 18:25.960
I got what I wanted.

18:27.100 --> 18:28.160
What's wrong?

18:35.510 --> 18:39.810
Who is that? I know her from somewhere...

18:40.510 --> 18:41.780
Mom!

18:42.350 --> 18:45.180
Hey, who made this inarizushi?

18:45.490 --> 18:47.580
It was Noboru.

18:47.650 --> 18:48.860
What? What's going on?

18:48.860 --> 18:54.160
Really?! Wow. He's good at cooking?
I'm so proud of him!

18:54.160 --> 18:54.960
How does it taste?!

18:55.100 --> 18:56.030
It's good.

18:56.030 --> 18:59.330
Lucky you. I wish I could try.

19:02.070 --> 19:04.470
Toru-chan. You can see me, right?

19:04.740 --> 19:10.570
Say, you have a birthmark that
looks like a scratch or welt, right?

19:11.450 --> 19:13.470
I have it, too.

19:17.950 --> 19:19.420
What about Noboru-chan?

19:20.190 --> 19:22.520
I don't think he does...

19:23.060 --> 19:26.860
I guess Noboru-chan takes after his father.

19:26.860 --> 19:31.490
Since you take after me, you're going
to grow up to be really handsome.

19:34.640 --> 19:36.240
Hurry up and get going.

19:36.240 --> 19:38.600
What? But I want to stay some more.

19:38.810 --> 19:41.240
You'll end up wandering again.

19:41.240 --> 19:44.440
Fine. I'm really going now! You really want that?

19:44.780 --> 19:46.680
Go, I said.

19:47.310 --> 19:48.910
Ku-chan...

19:49.750 --> 19:52.340
Fine, I'll go.

19:56.420 --> 19:58.820
Take care...

20:20.250 --> 20:24.550
The first words I said to her
were "I don't think he does."

20:24.550 --> 20:26.140
I feel so dumb.

20:26.890 --> 20:30.550
Why didn't I say more?

20:31.090 --> 20:33.650
There were so many things I wanted to say.

20:34.900 --> 20:38.350
I wished I could have called her "Mom."

20:41.470 --> 20:45.470
Um, why is Toru-san here crying?

20:45.470 --> 20:47.800
Probably because something touched his heart.

20:48.880 --> 20:52.940
Never mind him. I'm starving!

20:53.110 --> 20:55.050
Gimme food!

20:56.080 --> 20:57.140
You can have mine.

20:57.650 --> 20:59.240
Thanks for today.

20:59.450 --> 21:02.620
I haven't done anything. Well, maybe a little dance.

21:02.860 --> 21:03.580
Yeah...

21:04.020 --> 21:06.390
I danced because I wanted to.

21:07.060 --> 21:09.050
Yeah, I know.

21:09.830 --> 21:11.300
Smart boy.

21:29.380 --> 21:35.850
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:36.320 --> 21:43.530
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:44.900 --> 21:51.390
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

21:51.540 --> 21:59.170
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:00.080 --> 22:07.110
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:07.690 --> 22:14.180
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:14.430 --> 22:21.840
Daijoubu bokura wa hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:21.840 --> 22:29.480
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:29.480 --> 22:37.150
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:37.150 --> 22:48.360
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

22:55.870 --> 23:00.840
I was thinking of making those Japanese-style
misangas out of this and selling them.

23:00.840 --> 23:01.430
Sell them?

23:01.640 --> 23:05.750
They'll sell like hotcakes if I advertise 'em
as a talisman that wards off evil spirits...

23:05.750 --> 23:08.480
...since it's made from the fur
of the Kugen Fox of Mizuchi!

23:08.480 --> 23:10.540
It'll be great!

23:10.920 --> 23:17.460
My lord, is this the reason you instigated
Tenko-sama to perform the Spirit Passing?

23:17.460 --> 23:22.900
Of course. That fox would never give
me anything just because I asked.

23:25.000 --> 23:25.330
Next Time

23:25.330 --> 23:28.240
Next Time
Girls are always thinking about love.

23:28.240 --> 23:29.640
Next Time
What should I do?

23:29.640 --> 23:32.670
Next Time
The person I like is living with another cute girl.

23:32.670 --> 23:34.740
Next Time
Two of them, too!

23:34.740 --> 23:35.180
Next Time
Next episode, "Our Fox
Deity, Overindulges in Food."

23:35.180 --> 23:37.040
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Overindulges in Food
Next episode, "Our Fox
Deity, Overindulges in Food."

23:37.040 --> 23:39.480
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Overindulges in Food
Please don't be a two-timing jerk!

23:39.480 --> 23:39.950
Next Time
